<script lang="ts">
 import { onMount } from 'svelte'
 let {kind}:{kind:string}=$props()
 let mounted=$state(false), blur=$state(false), image=$state(true), backing=$state(true), crop=$state(false), reverse=$state(false), single=$state(false), missing=$state(false), palette=$state('categorical')
 onMount(()=>{mounted=true})
 const records=[{id:'A',value:30,tone:'.9'},{id:'B',value:70,tone:'.6'},{id:'C',value:50,tone:'.35'}]
 const shown=$derived(single?records.slice(0,1):records)
 const ordered=$derived(reverse?[...shown].reverse():shown)
</script>
<section class="task-study" data-study={kind} aria-label={kind==='hierarchy'?'Hierarchy diagnostic':kind==='image-text'?'Text over an image':'Stable data encoding'}>
<fieldset disabled={!mounted}><legend class="study-sr">Comparison controls</legend><div class="study-controls">
{#if kind==='hierarchy'}<label class="check"><input class="checkbox" type="checkbox" bind:checked={blur}/> Blur specimen only</label><label class="check"><input class="checkbox" type="checkbox" bind:checked={image}/> Show decorative image</label>
{:else if kind==='image-text'}<label class="check"><input class="checkbox" type="checkbox" bind:checked={backing}/> Stable text backing</label><label class="check"><input class="checkbox" type="checkbox" bind:checked={crop}/> Alternate crop</label>
{:else}<label>Encoding<select class="select" bind:value={palette}><option value="categorical">Categorical · group identity</option><option value="ordered">Ordered · magnitude</option><option value="diverging">Diverging · change from 50</option></select></label><button class="btn" onclick={()=>reverse=!reverse}>Reverse records</button><label class="check"><input class="checkbox" type="checkbox" bind:checked={single}/> One category</label><label class="check"><input class="checkbox" type="checkbox" bind:checked={missing}/> Missing B value</label>{/if}</div></fieldset>
{#if kind==='hierarchy'}<p>Intended first reading: the invitation to read the report. Compare its weight against the decorative image, then return to normal size.</p><div class="hierarchy-sample" class:blur><div class="hierarchy-image" class:absent={!image} aria-hidden="true">✳</div><h4>Read the field report</h4><p>Findings from a local study, with the methods and limitations available together.</p><span class="sample-action">Read report → (specimen label)</span></div><p>Blur changes only this noninteractive specimen. Normal-size reading and actual task testing remain necessary.</p>
{:else if kind==='image-text'}<div class="image-text-sample" class:crop><svg viewBox="0 0 400 200" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="400" height="200" fill="#e7e9e7"/><path d="M0 180L150 20 240 170 400 40V200H0Z" fill="#304f42"/></svg><p class:backing>Field report<br/><small>Text over an original schematic image</small></p></div><p>The alternate crop changes the region behind the same letters. A dark backing provides a stable pair; compare actual contrast before using an uncovered image in a product.</p>
{:else}<p>{palette==='categorical'?'A, B and C keep their assigned marks and tones through reordering.':palette==='ordered'?'Darker fill indicates a larger value; it does not identify a category.':'The specimen midpoint is 50 units. Signs and labels distinguish direction.'}</p><ul class="encoding-records">{#each ordered as record (record.id)}<li><strong>{record.id}</strong><span class="encoding-track" class:diverging={palette==='diverging'}>{#if !(missing&&record.id==='B')}<span data-category={record.id} style:width={`${palette==='diverging'?Math.abs(record.value-50):record.value}%`} style:inset-inline-start={palette==='diverging'?`${Math.min(record.value,50)}%`:'0'} style:opacity={palette==='categorical'?record.tone:palette==='ordered'?record.value/100:.8}></span>{/if}</span><span>{missing&&record.id==='B'?'Missing':`${palette==='diverging'?`${record.value-50>=0?'+':''}${record.value-50}`:record.value} units`}</span></li>{/each}</ul><p>Source: fixed local values A 30, B 70, C 50. Values and labels stay available without color. Diverging mode places zero change at the center; bars extend left for negative change and right for positive change. Missing is not zero.</p>{/if}
<noscript>Initial comparisons remain readable; switches require JavaScript.</noscript></section>
<style>
.hierarchy-sample{padding:16px;border-inline-start:2px solid var(--color-line-strong)}.hierarchy-sample.blur{filter:blur(3px)}.hierarchy-image{font-size:80px;line-height:1.2;text-align:center;background:var(--color-surface-inset);height:100px}.hierarchy-image.absent{visibility:hidden}.sample-action{font-weight:600}.image-text-sample{position:relative;overflow:hidden;height:200px}.image-text-sample svg{position:absolute;width:140%;height:100%;left:0}.image-text-sample.crop svg{left:-40%}.image-text-sample p{position:absolute;bottom:12px;left:12px;right:12px;color:white;padding:12px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.4}.image-text-sample p.backing{background:#15231e}.image-text-sample small{font-weight:400}.encoding-records{list-style:none;padding:0}.encoding-records li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1em minmax(0,1fr) 6em;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin:16px 0}.encoding-track{position:relative;height:18px;border:1px solid var(--color-line-strong)}.encoding-track span{position:absolute;display:block;height:100%;background:currentColor}
.encoding-track.diverging::after{content:"";position:absolute;left:50%;height:100%;border-left:1px solid currentColor}</style>
